    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/all_jobs.atom": {
      "title": "Ashland University: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:jobs.ashland.edu,2005:/postings/all_jobs Ashland University: All Jobs 2026-08-21T13:53:00-04:00 https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8754 2026-08-21T13:52:59-04:00 2026-08-21T13:53:00-04:00 Full-Time Grill Cook - Eagles Nest <ul><li>Prepare ala carte breakfast and lunch items for students, staff, and guests of Ashland University.</li><li>Set up breakfast station for the days orders and efficiently transition to lunch.</li><li>Maintain a clean and organized station throughout service.</li><li>Stock station and prep additional items as needed.</li><li>Maintain orders from Grubhub as well as in-house orders.</li><li>Assist in monthly Inventory counting and monitor stock rotation and expiration to minimize waste.</li><li>Ability to operate registers and take orders in a timely manner.</li><li>Assist with monthly inventory for cost of goods.</li><li>Maintain high levels of sanitation following the Ohio Revised Code for food safety.</li></ul> Eagle's Nest https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8669 2026-08-04T11:55:19-04:00 2026-08-04T11:55:20-04:00 Financial Aid Counselor - Financial Aid Office <div>The main functions of the Financial Aid Office are to effectively and comprehensively assist students and parents through the financial aid process and efficiently manage federal, state, and institutional financial aid programs. The Financial Aid Counselor provides financial aid services to undergraduate and graduate students as well as correctional education students across the country. The Financial Aid Counselor will be responsible for, but not limited to, conducting student needs analysis and preparing financial aid packages, reviewing verifications, determining eligibility, resolving conflicting information, resolving over-awards, performing professional judgement regarding eligibility, and facilitating problem solving with students, families, and other Ashland University employees.<br><br></div><ul><li>Conducts needs analysis in compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations and policies to determine relative eligibility of each financial aid applicant.</li><li>Determines the types and amounts of financial aid to be awarded to the student through the packaging process according to federal, state, and institutional requirements.</li><li>Counsels current and prospective undergraduate/graduate students and their parents through the application process in regards to financial aid programs, personal financial planning, and money management. Responsible for a section of undergraduate and graduate students based on the alphabet.</li><li>Resolves conflicting information, SARC codes, and over-awards.</li><li>Utilizes professional judgement to adjust a student’s eligibility based on documented mitigating circumstances in accordance with federal regulation.</li><li>Reviews completed verification for accuracy in compliance with federal regulations.</li><li>Completes return of Title IV Funds calculations.</li><li>Participates in the development of policies and procedures.</li><li>Participates in annual training and professional development.</li><li>Create, maintain, and present educational financial aid materials.</li><li>Complete other tasks as requested.</li></ul> Financial Aid https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8760 2026-08-21T15:19:32-04:00 2026-08-21T15:19:32-04:00 Head Women's Lacrosse Coach - Athletics <div>Ashland University is an NCAA Division II institution that competes in the Great Midwest Athletic Conference (GMAC). Ashland University offers a comprehensive 24-sport athletic program.</div><div>The university is located off of Interstate 71 in Ashland, Ohio, midway between Cleveland and Columbus.<br><br></div><ul><li>Candidates must be able to teach proper technique and skill development in various aspects of lacrosse. Candidates should have a complete and thorough understanding of the sport and be able to instruct student-athletes in small group and one-on-one settings.</li><li>Applicants should be well versed and able to instruct student-athletes on physical health, team concepts and team building exercises, team development techniques and safety.</li><li>A thorough understanding of NCAA and GMAC rules and regulations is required. The head coach must adhere to these rules and ensure that the program is in compliance with all rules, regulations and guidelines. The ability to articulate these to student-athletes is also required.</li><li>An understanding of Ashland University’s mission and goals is required. Applicants must have the ability to explain these to student-athletes.</li><li>Candidates will be responsible for monitoring the budget of the sport. All plans for travel and equipment purchase also fall under the responsibility of the head coach.</li><li>This position requires the ability to recruit potential student-athletes. The head coach is responsible for meeting all Ashland University roster requirements.</li><li>The head coach is responsible for monitoring academic progress of all student-athletes on the team and working with various constituencies across campus to ensure that student-athletes receive the proper academic counseling and assistance.</li><li>All practice and game preparation falls under the direction of the head coach. The head coach is responsible for the implementation of game plans and will be the lead coach at all games and tournaments.</li><li>The head coach will direct and finalize all scouting responsibilities.</li><li>The head coach will select and direct and evaluate a graduate assistant coach.</li><li>This position could require other assignments as assigned by the athletic director. These could include fundraising, game management and representing the athletic department at various functions.</li></ul> Athletics https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8682 2026-08-05T15:19:30-04:00 2026-08-05T15:19:30-04:00 Site Coordinator - South Central Correctional Center (Missouri) - Correctional Education <div>The Site Coordinator provides administrative support for Ashland University Correctional Education staff and students. The Site Coordinator reports directly to the designated Correctional Education State Director.<br><br></div><ul><li>Oversee daily operations at the assigned correctional facility(ies)/site(s) and represent the university in collaboration with the State Department of Corrections (DOC).</li><li>Act as the liaison between the facility staff, students, and Ashland University (AU).</li><li>Identify, screen and recruit students in alignment with Ashland University and DOC criteria.</li><li>Collaborate with the Student Success team through assisting students with completion of the AU application paperwork and digital submission process. Ensure students have access to their courses and remain accountable, while guiding them on how to address any questions or concerns.</li><li>Support students by assisting them in addressing issues and communications related to student access, i.e. end-user device is non-functional, out to court, transferred to a non-AU facility, lack of technological access, total lockdown at the facility, unexpected release.</li><li>Collaborate with the Financial Aid team whereby provide student support related to; the completion of the Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA), aid counseling, documentation requests, navigating the loan default process, satisfactory academic progress, and all other applicable requests from the AU Financial Aid team.</li><li>Collaborate with Academic Services through proctoring, recording and uploading tests, speeches and assignments as instructed to maximize student success. Assignments should be submitted on assigned due dates. If covering additional site locations, assignments should be submitted as close to assigned due dates as possible.</li><li>Provide students with an Ashland University orientation and academic correctional education processes and procedures before the semester begins.</li><li>Orders and manages site inventory of end user devices, student textbooks and instructional supplies. Provide timely, accurate inventory reports (textbooks and end-user devices) as assigned.</li><li>Ensure students have the necessary materials to participate in registered courses, including the distribution of end user devices, equipment, textbooks, and other educational materials.</li><li>Responsible for the distribution and collection of course evaluations and University assessments.</li><li>Organize and conduct student extracurricular activities such as but not limited to commencement and incentives.</li><li>Distribute Ashland University library research in a timely manner and in compliance with DOC regulations.</li><li>Identify students who will be releasing prior to completing their Ashland University degree, ensure students complete the required pre-release exit interview form, and encourage students to continue their education through the Ashland University re-entry program.</li><li>Maintains student privacy and record keeping according to the Family Education Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA).</li><li>Establish weekly meetings with each student regarding academic engagement, review participation reports, check end user device access, and encourage students.</li><li>Ensure compliance with AU policies, accreditation standards and DOC policies and procedures.</li></ul> Correctional Education Program https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8315 2026-05-06T12:31:40-04:00 2026-05-06T12:31:40-04:00 Casual Game Operations Staff - Athletics <div>The Ashland University Athletics Department is seeking reliable and responsible game operations staff for the academic year.<br><br></div><ul><li>Assist the department at a number of athletic contests and are an integral part of the operation.</li><li>Hours and days vary depending on game schedules.</li><li>Positions include but are not limited to: ushers, scoreboard operators, music, ball crew, gate attendants, ticket operations staff, etc.</li></ul> Athletics https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8796 2026-08-31T14:15:53-04:00 2026-08-31T14:15:53-04:00 Full-Time Salad Prep - Student Dining <ul><li>Covers days off for other employees. Schedule will vary from a.m. to p.m. along with every other weekend.</li><li>Duties include vegetable prep, salad composition, assembling catering trays<br>and salads.</li><li>Stocks and maintains raw ingredients for Student Dining salad bar.</li><li>May be required to work other positions based on staffing needs.</li></ul> Convocation Center (Student Dining) https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8694 2026-08-06T16:16:43-04:00 2026-08-06T16:16:44-04:00 Sales and Marketing Manager, Catering and Conferences <div>The Ashland University Catering and Conferences Sales and Marketing Manager will work directly with clients and potential clients to secure their business and plan events. This position will also work with internal AU clients to generate BEOs for their events. This position is also responsible for all print and digital marketing for Catering and Conferences including brochures, menus, website, social media, and email campaigns.<br><br></div><div><strong>Sales Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>·Lead venue tours with prospective clients.</li><li>Initiate and complete all sales follow-up for all leads including emails, calls, and reminders, including tracking in ClickUp.</li><li>Generate all food, beverages, linen, and décor details for all their booked events.</li><li>Manage all upselling and cross-selling programs, including décor, all-inclusive packages, and Eagle Custom merchandise.</li><li>Manage the AU Catering email account with the Director and respond to all catering inquiries received, excluding campus and conference inquiries.</li><li>Receive and respond to all website inquiries, excluding conference inquiries.</li><li>Attend bridal shows to promote AU Catering services and event venues.</li><li>Work with the Director and Chef to plan special university-hosted events such as YMBC Ladies Night, the Eagler Golf Outing, and other assigned events.</li><li>Collaborate with the Director of Catering and Conferences to develop new menus, packages, brochures, and pricing.</li><li>Generate all internal supply orders and maintain the supply order form with new items and annual pricing updates.</li><li>Coordinate repeat client bookings from year to year or for multi-year agreements.</li><li>Coordinate and conduct bridal and other large event tastings.</li><li>Support sales and marketing initiatives across other Auxiliary Services departments.</li><li>Propose and review approved quarterly Key Performance Indicators (KPIs).<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Marketing Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Create marketing materials and campaigns for catering special events, menus, brochures, and social media content consistent with Ashland University brand guidelines.</li><li>Manage the Catering website.</li><li>Manage all digital marketing content, including Catering Instagram, Facebook, and wedding/event website pages.</li><li>Design and produce both digital and print marketing materials.</li><li>Create and distribute all catering email marketing campaigns.</li><li>Conduct post-event follow-up with large event clients to gather feedback.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong>Other Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Generate Contracts for all external sold events.</li><li>Be present at the more demanding events sold like weddings and big conferences, at least until meal is served.</li><li>During summer seasons, assist the Director with Conference logistics when needed.</li><li>Review invoices weekly to confirm final client charges.</li><li>Submit RSVP reminders for upcoming clients.</li><li>Receive deposits and payments as needed when the Director is unavailable.</li><li>Place Connie Douglin Linen orders for booked events.</li><li>Supervise and direct event supervisors, setup workers, and other catering staff.</li></ul> Catering https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8319 2026-05-06T12:36:48-04:00 2026-05-06T12:36:48-04:00 Casual Catering Server - Catering and Conferences <div>Server for Catered Events including Wedding Receptions, Corporate Events, Lunch Meetings, and Off-Site events.<br><br></div> Catering https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8799 2026-08-31T14:37:08-04:00 2026-08-31T14:37:09-04:00 Part-Time Deli Server - Student Dining <ul><li>Set up Deli station in the morning.</li><li>Organize bread rack and resupply based on the the days requirements.</li><li>Stock coolers and fill condiment bottles for the day.</li><li>Maintain a clean and sanitary work station.</li><li>Position works Monday-Friday 8:00 a.m. - 2:30 p.m., 11:00 a.m. - 7:30 p.m. every other weekend.</li></ul> Convocation Center (Student Dining) https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8710 2026-08-17T10:07:50-04:00 2026-08-17T10:07:50-04:00 Casual Talon Transport Drivers - Student Affairs <div>Ashland University is seeking dependable, friendly drivers to join our <strong>Talon Transport</strong> team. Drivers provide transportation for students, faculty, and staff to destinations throughout Ohio, including airports, medical appointments, internships, government offices, and more. If you enjoy driving and making a difference in the student experience, we'd love to hear from you!<br><br></div><div><strong>Position Details:</strong></div><ul><li>Flexible, ride-based schedule—claim trips that fit your availability.</li><li>Minimum commitment of <strong>2 rides per month.</strong></li><li>Drive a university-owned SUV covered by AU insurance.</li></ul> International Student Services https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8324 2026-05-06T12:42:41-04:00 2026-05-06T12:42:42-04:00 Casual Crew Member - Student Dining <div>Various positions throughout the Food Service Operations</div> Convocation Center (Student Dining) https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8839 2026-09-04T12:24:01-04:00 2026-09-04T12:24:01-04:00 Full-Time Safety Services Officer - Safety Services <div>The Safety Services Officer position is under the direct supervision of the Director of Safety Services who reports to the Vice President of Management and Planning . Because officers occasionally cover shifts for or provide coverage for dispatchers during breaks, officers are expected to be effective in performing dispatcher duties as well. Officers are cross-trained in this regard and are expected to stay current on dispatching responsibilities.<br><br></div><ul><li>Maintain satisfactory attendance and punctuality.</li><li>Support the mission, goals and objectives of AU and the department.</li><li>Assist the campus community in a constructive, effective and positive manner.</li><li>Report safety concerns to the director.</li><li>Initiate emergency response as necessary.</li><li>Notify the director of scheduling conflicts.</li><li>Maintain departmental confidentiality.</li><li>At the start of each shift:<ul><li>review daily assignment sheet</li><li>get current information from previous shift staff</li><li>check for updates (i.e. notes on message board, etc.) &amp; review logs</li></ul></li><li>Cover for dispatcher breaks and shifts as needed.</li><li>Immediately assist all officers when called for assistance or during emergencies.</li><li>Respond to all service calls with urgency.</li><li>Uphold the policies of the university.</li><li>Conduct walk through of university buildings.</li><li>Lock, unlock and check facilities in a thorough manner.</li><li>Use proper radio codes and language.</li><li>Provide detailed written reports for incidents requiring documentation.</li><li>Provide immediate follow up with all parties for incidents by conducting and documenting interviews.</li><li>Notify the police for situations requiring their assistance (i.e. illegal drug activity on campus, incident involving a weapon, etc.).</li><li>Perform basic emergency locksmith related duties for campus (i.e. core changes).</li><li>Maintain departmental equipment (and offices) in a safe, clean and organized manner and any other task(s) as directed by supervisors.</li></ul> Safety Services https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8714 2026-08-17T11:48:57-04:00 2026-08-17T11:48:57-04:00 Director of Student Activities - Office of Student & Residence Life <div>As a key member of Student Life and Success at Ashland University, the Director of Student Activities is responsible for creating significant opportunities for student engagement that foster a sense of belonging, learning and personal/professional growth, while also aiding in student retention.<br><br></div><ul><li>Coordinate/plan, implement and evaluate traditional campus-wide events including the Involvement Fair, Welcome Tent, Week of Welcome, Homecoming, and Springfest, among others.</li><li>Advise the Campus Activities Board, the primary student programming organization. Primary responsibilities include supervision, selection, contract negotiation, program implementation and evaluation. In addition, the advisor assists in recruitment, selection, training, and holistic development of CAB members and attends campus events.</li><li>Advise the Technical Productions Crew, the student led organization whose main function is to provide sound, stage and lighting for campus programs.</li><li>Advise the Activities, Budgeting, and Chartering Committee (ABCC) of Student Senate on matters of chartering and funding. Serve as historian and non-voting member.</li><li>Provide budget oversight for all student organization funding.</li><li>Serve as the staff liaison for 100+ student organizations. Implement annual processes including roster updates to Engage, provisional and full charter applications, and funding requests, etc.</li><li>Maintain Student Organization Manual.</li><li>Create, implement, and assess training for student organizations to include student organization policies, procedures, and utilization of Engage Ashland software.</li><li>Manage Engage Ashland software, Engage Ashland Instagram account and create publicity materials to increase use of these platforms. Approve events and forms submitted through Engage.</li><li>Manage Student Organization Resource Room and all event supplies.</li><li>Host Programming Team meetings and maintain programming calendar.</li><li>Assist with Orientation programs and serve as support during the implementation of orientation initiatives, including June/July Summer Orientation Days and Orientation Weekend.</li><li>Co-facilitate annual Hazing Prevention training session during Orientation Weekend.</li><li>Plan and facilitate annual Leadership &amp; Service awards program.</li><li>Attend annual NACA conference with a student delegation.</li><li>Supervise undergraduate intern.</li><li>Serve on Strategic Planning Team, Theme 3B: Modernize and reimagine residential living and programming to enhance recruitment, retention, and student satisfaction.</li><li>Other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Student Life https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8842 2026-09-04T13:17:53-04:00 2026-09-04T13:17:54-04:00 2nd Shift Building Service Worker - Building Services <ul><li>Cleaning and maintaining living facilities, dining areas, laundry areas, restrooms, shower areas, classrooms and offices.</li><li>Replenishing soap and paper products.</li><li>Removing trash and recycling from buildings while replacing liners in the trash and recycling containers.</li><li>Sweeping, mopping and cleaning floors and stairwells.</li><li>Vacuuming and shampooing carpeted areas.</li><li>Dusting furniture, washing walls and windows.</li><li>Cleaning outside steps and entryways (may include snow removal from entryways).</li><li>Moving heavy furniture, supplies and equipment.</li><li>Burnishing, refinishing and stripping tile and terrazzo flooring.</li><li>Reporting items in need of repair and ordering supplies.</li><li>Performing related or special duties as assigned by a supervisor.</li></ul> Building Services https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8326 2026-05-06T12:47:49-04:00 2026-05-06T12:47:49-04:00 Casual Dish Room - Student Dining <div>Assist other crew members in the Dish Room during meal service which can include:</div><ul><li>Sorting silverware</li><li>Breaking down meal trays to be washed</li><li>Loading dish machine</li><li>Unloading dish machine</li><li>Putting dishes, pots and pans in the appropriate areas</li><li>Assist with catered meal dishes</li><li>Cleaning dish room at the end of the shift</li></ul> Convocation Center (Student Dining) https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8730 2026-08-19T10:57:20-04:00 2026-08-19T10:57:21-04:00 Staff Accountant - Business Office <div>The Staff Accountant supports the daily financial operations of the Business Office by processing transactions, maintaining records, and ensuring documentation is complete and accurate in accordance with established policies and procedures.<br><br></div><ul><li>Administer and support the University purchasing card (P-Card) program, including card issuance, training, policy compliance monitoring, review of supporting documentation, and reconciliation of transactions.</li><li>Review purchasing card and employee expense activity to ensure compliance with University policies, internal controls, and applicable regulations.</li><li>Provide guidance and customer service to faculty, staff, and departmental budget managers regarding accounting procedures, purchasing card usage, account coding, and financial policies.</li><li>Perform monthly reconciliations of assigned balance sheet and income statement accounts and investigate and resolve discrepancies in a timely manner.</li><li>Maintain the integrity of the general ledger through accurate recording, analysis, and documentation of financial transactions.</li><li>Assist with month-end and year-end closing processes, including account analysis, accrual entries, reconciliations, and preparation of supporting schedules.</li><li>Record and/or required journal entries, accruals and reclassifications for the monthly, quarterly, and year-end closing processes.</li><li>Process the allocation of departmental costs, such as telephone, postage, and copies with the assistance of student workers.</li><li>Assist and prepare financial reports, account analyses, and supporting documentation for management review.</li><li>Assist with annual audits by preparing work papers, schedules, account reconciliations, and responding to auditor requests.</li><li>Assist with special projects, process improvement initiatives, financial system testing, and other duties as assigned.</li><li>Ability to work after hours and weekends as needed.</li><li>Other Duties as assigned or requested by the Controller and Assistant Controller.</li></ul> Business Office https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8601 2026-07-13T16:37:32-04:00 2026-07-13T16:37:32-04:00 Part-Time PM Swing Shift - Student Dining <div>Responsible for working multiple points of service, relieving employees on days off in the following serving positions:<br><br></div><ul><li>Daily Special</li><li>Dining Attendant</li><li>Pizza</li><li>Pasta</li><li>Deli</li><li>Salad Bar</li><li>Dessert</li></ul><div><br>Position is scheduled Monday – Friday and every other weekend.</div> Convocation Center (Student Dining) https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8740 2026-08-21T10:48:54-04:00 2026-08-21T10:48:54-04:00 Lyceum Café Lead - Lyceum Café <ul><li>Must be available 7:30 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. Monday through Friday.</li><li>This is a part time, 10-month position (August-May). Position works an average of 34 hrs. per week.</li><li>Hands-on position assisting the Lyceum Café Manager with daily production needs for our customers.</li><li>Production of multiple specialty coffee drinks.</li><li>Assist with ordering, stocking, monitoring food quality and sanitation of the facility.</li><li>Maintain register and balancing of the cash drawer daily.</li><li>Monitor student labor and hours.</li><li>Assist manager with any scheduling needs.</li><li>Part-time position includes prorated vacation leave, sick leave, and holiday pay only.</li></ul> Lyceum Café https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8604 2026-07-13T16:40:36-04:00 2026-07-13T16:40:37-04:00 Part-Time AM Swing Shift - Student Dining <div>Responsible for working multiple points of service, relieving employees on days off in the following serving positions:</div><ul><li>Daily Special</li><li>Dining Attendant</li><li>Pizza</li><li>Pasta</li><li>Deli</li><li>Salad Bar</li><li>Dessert</li></ul> Convocation Center (Student Dining) https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8752 2026-08-21T13:50:37-04:00 2026-08-21T13:50:37-04:00 Admissions Representative - Undergraduate Admissions <div>The Admissions Representative - Undergraduate Admissions position assists prospective students and their parents interested in Ashland University through the enrollment process, and to coordinate all college fairs and travel for Undergraduate Admissions, and create communication for those who influence first-year students.<br><br></div><ul><li>Serves as the primary contact for prospective traditional first-year students and their influencers within specific geographic recruitment area.</li><li>Travels to visit high schools in assigned recruitment area.</li><li>Travels to attend college day/night programs within assigned recruitment area.</li><li>Hosts virtual college information programs in targeted recruitment areas.</li><li>Assists with campus visit programs throughout the year.</li><li>Serves as a liaison to the Ashbrook and Honors programs.</li><li>Serves as a liaison to the Office of Student Success.</li><li>Serves as a liaison to the College of Arts &amp; Sciences and other campus offices for new student recruitment purposes.</li><li>Serves as a member of the Office of Admissions Leadership Team.</li><li>Conducts on-campus personal visits and group visit presentations for prospective students and their guests.</li><li>Assists Director of Admissions with data analysis through utilization of Othot &amp; Slate, including weekly enrollment reporting.</li><li>Responsible for knowledge of the Slate CRM for communication with prospective students.</li><li>Effective interpersonal and public speaking communication skills.</li><li>Willingness to work evenings, weekends or as needed.</li><li>Ability to work unsupervised.</li><li>Ability to understand and utilize various technology tools for student recruitment and data analytics.</li><li>Commitment to diversity and inclusion.</li><li>Evidence of collaboration within a campus community.</li><li>Able to communicate with a wide variety of individuals both on and off campus.</li><li>Willingness to travel extensively during the fall and spring months.</li><li>Responsible for knowledge of the Slate CRM for communication with prospective students.</li></ul> Admissions https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8658 2026-07-28T13:57:58-04:00 2026-07-28T13:57:58-04:00 Administrative Assistant to the Director - Columbus Center <div>This full-time position is under the supervision of, and reports to, the Director of Professional Learning Services (PLS). The Administrative Assistant provides support services to PLS. The Administrative Assistant reports directly to the Director of PLS at the Ashland University Columbus, OH Center.<br><br></div><ul><li>Completes administrative office and clerical work including serving as a resource person to inform interested individuals about PLS.</li><li>Assigns and maintains class numbering system and database.</li><li>Prepares and forwards agreement forms to school districts and vendors.</li><li>Enters registrations into computer system.</li><li>Processes credit/debit card and check payments.</li><li>Balances payment records and forwards to business office.</li><li>Maintains files on grade sheets, syllabi, and contracts.</li><li>Creates and updates the class schedule on the web page.</li><li>Updates and maintains the web page information.</li><li>Responds daily to e-mail communications.</li><li>Prepares reports under the direction of the Director.</li><li>Demonstrates necessary' human relations skills in order to maintain a friendly, helpful atmosphere working with instructors, students, and school district personnel.</li><li>Maintains current and accurate records on the computer.</li><li>Maintains sufficient office supplies/forms for PLS.</li><li>Prepares regular mailings to superintendents, curriculum directors, adjuncts, and others for PLS via US Mail and e-mail.</li><li>Processes check requests and supplement contracts for PLS.</li><li>Performs other duties requested by the Director.</li></ul> Professional Learning https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8757 2026-08-21T13:57:57-04:00 2026-08-21T13:57:57-04:00 Site Coordinator - Chillicothe Correctional Institution (Ohio) - Correctional Education <div>The Site Coordinator provides administrative support for Ashland University Correctional Education staff and students. The Site Coordinator reports directly to the designated Correctional Education State Director.<br><br></div><ul><li>Oversee daily operations at the assigned correctional facility(ies)/site(s) and represent the university in collaboration with the State Department of Corrections (DOC).</li><li>Act as the liaison between the facility staff, students, and Ashland University (AU).</li><li>Identify, screen and recruit students in alignment with Ashland University and DOC criteria.</li><li>Collaborate with the Student Success team through assisting students with completion of the AU application paperwork and digital submission process. Ensure students have access to their courses and remain accountable, while guiding them on how to address any questions or concerns.</li><li>Support students by assisting them in addressing issues and communications related to student access, i.e. end-user device is non-functional, out to court, transferred to a non-AU facility, lack of technological access, total lockdown at the facility, unexpected release.</li><li>Collaborate with the Financial Aid team whereby provide student support related to; the completion of the Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA), aid counseling, documentation requests, navigating the loan default process, satisfactory academic progress, and all other applicable requests from the AU Financial Aid team.</li><li>Collaborate with Academic Services through proctoring, recording and uploading tests, speeches and assignments as instructed to maximize student success. Assignments should be submitted on assigned due dates. If covering additional site locations, assignments should be submitted as close to assigned due dates as possible.</li><li>Provide students with an Ashland University orientation and academic correctional education processes and procedures before the semester begins.</li><li>Orders and manages site inventory of end user devices, student textbooks and instructional supplies. Provide timely, accurate inventory reports (textbooks and end-user devices) as assigned.</li><li>Ensure students have the necessary materials to participate in registered courses, including the distribution of end user devices, equipment, textbooks, and other educational materials.</li><li>Responsible for the distribution and collection of course evaluations and University assessments.</li><li>Organize and conduct student extracurricular activities such as but not limited to commencement and incentives.</li><li>Distribute Ashland University library research in a timely manner and in compliance with DOC regulations.</li><li>Identify students who will be releasing prior to completing their Ashland University degree, ensure students complete the required pre-release exit interview form, and encourage students to continue their education through the Ashland University re-entry program.</li><li>Maintains student privacy and record keeping according to the Family Education Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA).</li><li>Establish weekly meetings with each student regarding academic engagement, review participation reports, check end user device access, and encourage students.</li><li>Ensure compliance with AU policies, accreditation standards and DOC policies and procedures.</li></ul> Correctional Education Program https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8676 2026-08-04T15:35:36-04:00 2026-08-04T15:35:37-04:00 Seminary Grants Finance & Compliance Manager - Ashland Theological Seminary <div>Ashland Theological Seminary (ATS) equips modern‑day disciples to serve as leaders and counselors in diverse ministry and professional contexts. The ATS Grants team supports this mission by cultivating partnerships, designing and delivering high-quality non-academic programming, and stewarding grant funding for strategic innovation and institutional learning. Our current portfolio includes programs focused on clergy and clergy family well‑being; rural ministry and community resilience; courageous preaching; and seminary education and business‑model innovation. The team manages nearly $5M in active awards along with significant leverage commitments.<br><br></div><div>The Grants Finance &amp; Compliance Manager provides leadership for finance operations across the ATS Grants portfolio, working closely with the Program Director, university counterparts, external partners, and other team members to manage risk, strengthen practice, and support sound financial performance. A key responsibility includes developing and launching a Rural and Small Towns microgrants mechanism capable of issuing 70+ small grants annually. We seek a candidate with experience in grants or nonprofit financial management, strong analytical skills, and demonstrated ability to build and maintain fit‑for‑purpose financial systems for teams or business units with multiple stakeholders.<br><br></div><ul><li>Lead monthly financial projections, burn-rate analyses, and reconciliations across the portfolio. Identify gaps in current expenditure and grant financial management practices and develop tools/templates that enhance grant performance.</li><li>Maintain accurate, audit-ready documentation and ensure that financial practices follow internal controls, procurement standards, and award/subaward terms and conditions. Prepare timely, accurate, and compliant financial reports for internal leadership and external funders.</li><li>Partner with the Program Director to design and launch a microgrants mechanism capable of issuing seventy plus (70+) awards annually. Select and configure appropriate software and establish processes in collaboration with University stakeholders to handle efficient disbursements and compliance tracking.</li><li>Provide financial and compliance oversight and monitoring of subgrantees, microgrant recipients, and key vendors; identify and track emerging risks; and work with the Program Director to manage risks and resolve issues.</li><li>Manage documentation and accounting for all leverage commitments across the portfolio ($2M). Document and verify matches in real-time to ensure institutional compliance.</li><li>Offer targeted training to seminary staff, partners, and microgrant recipients on compliance expectations and financial best practices.</li><li>Serve as a key partner to the Program Director in portfolio-wide planning, risk identification and management, and scenario modeling. Manage key relationships with University stakeholders and external partners.<br><br></li></ul><div><strong><em>This is a grant-funded and term-limited staff position (not a contract role), funded through December 31, 2029. We are happy to discuss what this means with candidates.</em></strong></div> Seminary https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8766 2026-08-24T15:40:16-04:00 2026-08-24T15:40:17-04:00 Principal Faculty for the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies- Part Time - Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences <div>The Part-Time Principal Faculty member for the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies Program will work closely with the Program Director and Principal Faculty members to implement and maintain the curriculum in accordance with ARC-PA Standards as a course director on a twelve (12) month, part-time basis. As a Course Director the individual is responsible for development, implementation, delivery, and evaluation of assigned courses. The Principal Faculty works collaboratively with faculty within the Dwight Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences and Ashland University.<br><br>The Part-Time Principal Faculty member is responsible for course development and implementation to ensure the PA students readiness to practice upon graduation.<br><br></div><div><strong>Principal Faculty member responsibilities include:</strong></div><ul><li>Support the mission of Ashland University and Dwight Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences.</li><li>Support Ashland University’s philosophy of <em>Accent on the Individual.</em></li><li>Development and review of the mission statement of the PA Program.</li><li>Provide academic instruction.</li><li>Participates in review and revision of the program competencies.</li><li>Develops, implements, evaluates and ensures course syllabi maintain compliance with ARC-PA Standards of assigned courses.</li><li>Review and revision, as necessary, of the program goals and competencies.</li><li>Participates in developing, reviewing, and revising as necessary the mission statement for the program.</li><li>Participates in evaluating student performances.</li><li>Participate in the program’s ongoing self-assessment, analysis, and accreditation processes with primary responsibility for didactic education components.</li><li>Is familiar with ARC-PA accreditation standards and assists in providing documented compliance.</li><li>Participate in the development and maintenance of the didactic year sections of the student handbook.</li><li>Participate in the design and implementation of summative examinations.</li><li>Serve as an academic advisor to students.</li><li>Provide remedial instruction of didactic year students.<