privacy and record keeping according to the Family Education Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA).</li><li>Establish weekly meetings with each student regarding academic engagement, review participation reports, check end user device access, and encourage students.</li><li>Ensure compliance with AU policies, accreditation standards and DOC policies and procedures.</li></ul> Correctional Education Program https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8316 2026-05-06T12:32:44-04:00 2026-05-06T12:32:45-04:00 Casual Athletic Communications Game Day Staff - Athletics <div>The Ashland University Athletics Department is seeking reliable and responsible statistics staff for home games for the academic year.<br><br></div><ul><li>Help keep statistics at home football, soccer, volleyball, basketball, baseball, softball and women's lacrosse games.</li><li>Input statistics into stat computer using NCAA LiveStats and Presto.</li><li>Help spot for inputter at home games.</li></ul> Athletics https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8797 2026-08-31T14:22:34-04:00 2026-08-31T14:22:35-04:00 Desktop Engineer - Information Technology <div>The Desktop Engineer is a forward-thinking IT professional responsible for ensuring optimal desktop and endpoint operations across our diverse environment. This role not only covers traditional desktop support but also integrates modern endpoint management practices including cloud and mobile device management (MDM), cybersecurity fundamentals, and server-level administration. The successful candidate will be proficient in managing environments that leverage tools such as Microsoft Intune, Autopilot, JAMF for Apple device management, and traditional systems like Active Directory, Entra, and Azure. They will work collaboratively with IT peers, security teams, and client services to ensure that computer images, software deployments, and system customizations meet the highest standards of reliability, scalability, and security, in line with NIST guidelines and industry best practices.<br><br></div><ul><li><strong>Desktop and Endpoint Management</strong><ul><li>Create, maintain, and deploy modern computer images for Windows and Mac OS environments.</li><li>Manage and update endpoint devices using both traditional systems (e.g., Jira, JAMF) and modern cloud-based tools (e.g., Microsoft Intune).</li><li>Manage Windows Autopilot</li><li>Oversee mobile device management (MDM) practices to ensure secure and efficient management of enterprise mobile devices.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Cloud and Server Administration</strong><ul><li>Manage cloud applications and enforce cloud app security protocols.</li><li>Execute lower-level system administrator duties, including server patching, customizations, and routine maintenance.</li><li>Administer and maintain Active Directory, Entra, and Azure environments to support organizational infrastructure.</li><li>Help support the Hyper-V server environment and infrastructure.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Cybersecurity and Compliance</strong><ul><li>Integrate cybersecurity practices into daily operations, ensuring compliance with NIST standards and industry best practices.</li><li>Collaborate with cybersecurity teams to implement machine hardening, secure patching, and proactive vulnerability management.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Automation, Scripting, and System Updates</strong><ul><li>Develop and execute scripts (using PowerShell and other scripting languages) to automate routine tasks and OS setting adjustments.</li><li>Maintain a comprehensive update schedule for operating systems and applications, ensuring timely patching and customization.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Technical Support and Documentation</strong><ul><li>Respond to user tickets regarding software deployment, device management, and system updates, providing excellent end-user support.</li><li>Analyze the impact of proposed technology changes and document policies, procedures, and technical guides.</li><li>Train and mentor junior IT staff, serving as a role model and technical resource within the team.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Cross-Functional Collaboration and Process Improvement</strong><ul><li>Work closely with IT support, security, networking, and other project teams to develop and implement scalable technology solutions.</li><li>Identify and recommend process improvements to enhance the overall efficiency, security, and reliability of IT operations.</li><li>Foster strong working relationships with stakeholders, ensuring that IT solutions align with both business and educational objectives.</li></ul></li></ul> Information Technology https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8695 2026-08-06T16:23:39-04:00 2026-08-06T16:23:40-04:00 Full-Time Building Service Worker - Building Services <ul><li>Cleaning and maintaining living facilities, dining areas, laundry areas, restrooms, shower areas, classrooms and offices.</li><li>Replenishing soap and paper products.</li><li>Removing trash and recycling from buildings while replacing liners in the trash and recycling containers.</li><li>Sweeping, mopping and cleaning floors and stairwells.</li><li>Vacuuming and shampooing carpeted areas.</li><li>Dusting furniture, washing walls and windows.</li><li>Cleaning outside steps and entryways (may include snow removal from entryways).</li><li>Moving heavy furniture, supplies and equipment.</li><li>Burnishing, refinishing and stripping tile and terrazzo flooring.</li><li>Reporting items in need of repair and ordering supplies.</li><li>Performing related or special duties as assigned by a supervisor.</li></ul> Building Services https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8320 2026-05-06T12:38:15-04:00 2026-05-06T12:38:16-04:00 Casual Bartender - Catering & Conferences <div>Bartender for catered events such as wedding receptions, corporate holiday parties, and University functions. Bartenders set up and pull their own bars for each event. All bars are mobile, requiring the pulling and restocking of all alcohol, mixers, and garnishes before and after each event. Bartenders serve cocktails, beer, and wine.</div> Catering https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8826 2026-09-02T15:17:49-04:00 2026-09-02T15:17:49-04:00 Part-Time Administrative Assistant - Ashbrook Center <div>We are seeking a dependable, organized, and proactive Part-Time Administrative Assistant to support the day-to-day operations of the Ashbrook Center. The ideal candidate is a self-starter who can work independently, prioritize responsibilities, and provide professional and welcoming support to staff, interns, and visitors.<br><strong><br>Duties include, but are not limited to:</strong></div><ul><li>Answer the main phone line, take messages, and disseminate information to appropriate staff.</li><li>Order office and kitchen supplies and monitor inventory levels to ensure needed items are available.</li><li>Monitor interns and assist with assigning and coordinating their workload.</li><li>Welcome and assist visitors by providing directions, answering questions, and connecting them with appropriate personnel.</li><li>Manage incoming and outgoing USPS mail and UPS packages.</li><li>Work with related departments to execute tasks and provide administrative support as needed.</li><li>Ensure the smooth and efficient operation of the Ashbrook workroom and intern suite.</li><li>Perform other administrative duties and special projects as assigned.</li></ul> Ashbrook https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8712 2026-08-17T10:49:11-04:00 2026-08-17T10:49:12-04:00 Site Coordinator, Grafton Correctional Institution and Grafton Reintegration Center (Ohio) - Correctional Education <div>The Site Coordinator provides administrative support for Ashland University Correctional Education staff and students. The Site Coordinator reports directly to the designated Correctional Education State Director.<br><br></div><ul><li>Oversee daily operations at the assigned correctional facility(ies)/site(s) and represent the university in collaboration with the State Department of Corrections (DOC).</li><li>Act as the liaison between the facility staff, students, and Ashland University (AU).</li><li>Identify, screen and recruit students in alignment with AU and DOC criteria.</li><li>Collaborate with the Student Success team through assisting students with completion of the AU application paperwork and digital submission process. Ensure students have access to their courses and remain accountable, while guiding them on how to address any questions or concerns.</li><li>Support students by assisting them in addressing issues and communications related to student access, i.e. end-user device is non-functional, out to court, transferred to a non-AU facility, lack of technological access, total lockdown at the facility, unexpected release.</li><li>Collaborate with the Financial Aid team whereby provide student support related to; the completion of the Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA), aid counseling, documentation requests, navigating the loan default process, satisfactory academic progress, and all other applicable requests from the AU Financial Aid team.</li><li>Collaborate with Academic Services through proctoring, recording and uploading tests, speeches and assignments as instructed to maximize student success. Assignments should be submitted on assigned due dates. If covering additional site locations, assignments should be submitted as close to assigned due dates as possible.</li><li>Provide students with AU orientation and academic correctional education processes and procedures before the semester begins.</li><li>Orders and manages site inventory of end user devices, student textbooks and instructional supplies. Provide timely, accurate inventory reports (textbooks and end-user devices) as assigned.</li><li>Ensure students have the necessary materials to participate in registered courses, including the distribution of end user devices, equipment, textbooks, and other educational materials.</li><li>Responsible for the distribution and collection of course evaluations and University assessments.</li><li>Organize and conduct student extracurricular activities such as but not limited to commencement and incentives.</li><li>Distribute Ashland University library research in a timely manner and in compliance with DOC regulations.</li><li>Identify students who will be releasing prior to completing their AU degree, ensure students complete the required pre-release exit interview form, and encourage students to continue their education through the AU re-entry program.</li><li>Maintains student privacy and record keeping according to the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act (FERPA).</li><li>Establish weekly meetings with each student regarding academic engagement, review participation reports, check end user device access, and encourage students.</li><li>Ensure compliance with AU policies, accreditation standards and DOC policies and procedures.</li></ul> Correctional Education Program https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8325 2026-05-06T12:45:10-04:00 2026-05-06T12:45:11-04:00 Part-Time AM Pasta Server - Student Dining <ul><li>Prepare pasta, sauces, breadsticks, and toppings needed for daily production.</li><li>Complete related paperwork to document accurate product usage, and temp logs.</li><li>Maintain safe food temperatures throughout meal period.</li><li>Rotation of product, clean up and sanitation of area during and after shift.</li><li>Perform other duties as requested by management.</li><li>7:00 a.m. – 1:30 p.m. Monday-Friday; every other weekend 11:00 a.m. – 7:30 p.m.</li></ul> Convocation Center (Student Dining) https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8840 2026-09-04T12:24:48-04:00 2026-09-04T12:24:48-04:00 Full-Time 3rd Shift Custodian - Student Dining <ul><li>Scheduled shift 6:30 p.m. to 3:00 a.m. Includes every other weekend.</li><li>Sweep and mop the university’s Convocation Center kitchen and service area as well as the Eagles Nest kitchen and dining areas.</li><li>Clean exhaust hoods in both areas on a quarterly rotation.</li><li>Remove trash and recycling from facility.</li><li>Clean and stock restrooms.</li><li>Wax and buff floors on an annual basis.</li><li>Along with the other team members, responsible for the general cleanliness and sanitation of the facility.</li><li>Schedule varies in the summer based on conference groups.</li><li>Shovel snow and salt around entrance during inclement weather.</li><li>Any other duties assigned by your immediate supervisor.</li></ul> Convocation Center (Student Dining) https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8726 2026-08-17T16:19:24-04:00 2026-08-17T16:19:25-04:00 Discovery Development Officer - Institutional Advancement <div>Ashland University seeks a motivated and relationship-focused <strong>Discovery Development Officer (DXO)</strong> to join the Institutional Advancement team. This frontline fundraising position plays a vital role in building the University's pipeline of future leadership and major gift donors by identifying, researching, qualifying, and engaging alumni, parents, and friends with the capacity and interest to support Ashland University's mission.<br><br></div><div>The Discovery Development Officer serves as the first point of contact in the major gift fundraising process, conducting proactive outreach and discovery conversations to determine philanthropic interest and readiness for further engagement. Qualified prospects are strategically transitioned to Major Gift Officers for cultivation and solicitation.<br><br><strong>Essential Responsibilities</strong></div><ul><li>Identify, research, and qualify prospective leadership and major gift donors.</li><li>Conduct discovery outreach through phone calls, email, virtual meetings, and occasional in-person visits.</li><li>Build and manage an active portfolio of prospective donors and advance them through the qualification process.</li><li>Maintain accurate prospect records, contact reports, and next steps within the University's CRM.</li><li>Prepare prospect research, briefing materials, and travel recommendations for Major Gift Officers.</li><li>Collaborate with Advancement Services, Prospect Management, and frontline fundraisers to strengthen the donor pipeline.</li><li>Analyze prospect data, giving history, engagement, and wealth screening information to identify new fundraising opportunities.</li><li>Represent Ashland University professionally while building meaningful relationships with alumni, parents, and friends.</li><li>Support Institutional Advancement events and initiatives as needed.</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned.</li></ul> Development https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8844 2026-09-04T13:24:49-04:00 2026-09-04T13:24:49-04:00 Part-Time Catering Cook - Catering and Conferences <ul><li>Assist catering chef with production and service of catered events on and off campus.</li><li>Hours are varied due to timing of catered events.</li><li>Part-time position eligible for vacation, sick, and holiday pay.</li></ul> Catering https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8438 2026-06-02T12:03:02-04:00 2026-06-02T12:03:03-04:00 Nurse Practitioner - Student Health Center <div>This primary care provider works collaboratively with a multidisciplinary team responsible for the provision of quality health care services for students of Ashland University in accordance with standards of professional practice and ethical conduct. This team member provides clinical assessment, diagnosis and treatment for Ashland University students who are seen as patients in the Student Health Center. This is a 9-month position with full-time benefits.<br><br></div><ul><li>Assume ongoing responsibility for the primary care of Ashland University students' health needs.</li><li>Provide diagnosis, treatment and follow-up management of common acute illness and injuries and management of stable chronic conditions.</li><li>Promote health and wellness in areas of lifestyle and behavior that enhance physical, psychological, spiritual and social well-being.</li><li>Document appropriate, accurate and complete information in the student's medical record, in accordance with current Student Health Center policies and procedures.</li><li>Consult with his/her collaborating/supervising physician in an appropriate and timely manner when indicated or required by law.</li><li>Refer students to collaborating/supervising physician, other health care providers or relevant community agencies, when indicated.</li><li>Serve as preceptor for Athletic Training students.</li><li>Provide evaluation, treatment and/or referral of employee occupational injuries.</li><li>Maintain strict confidentiality of clinical, social, financial or other student/staff data in compliance with university, state and federal guidelines.</li><li>Communicate effectively with students, parents, physicians and colleagues.</li><li>Seek opportunities to promote professional and personal growth through available continuing educational activities.</li><li>Review and maintain Standard Care Arrangement/Physician Supervisory Plan with collaborating/supervising physician on an annual basis (or as required by law).</li><li>Demonstrate behavior which reflects a positive image of the Student Health Center and the University.</li><li>Demonstrate team member behaviors.</li><li>Serve on division and institution-wide committees as assigned.</li></ul> Health Center https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8735 2026-08-19T12:32:48-04:00 2026-08-19T12:32:49-04:00 Assistant Professor of Biblical Studies - Ashland Theological Seminary <div>Ashland Theological Seminary (ATS) is a graduate division of Ashland University, located in Ashland, Ohio. The position is a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Biblical Studies. This nine-month position begins on <strong>August 23, 2027</strong>.<br><br></div><div><strong>Ethos of Ashland Theological Seminary</strong></div><div>ATS was founded by the Brethren Church, whose Anabaptist and Pietist heritage shapes the core values of the Seminary. The Seminary is an evangelical and ecumenical institution, as well as a community of faith whose identity is shaped by its service to the scholarly community, the church, and the world. We embrace a diversity that finds its unity in Jesus Christ. We are committed to practicing justice in our engagement with one another and with the world. As partners in ministry and brothers and sisters in Christ, we strive to foster a redemptive community that lives by the values of God's kingdom.<br><br></div><div>Agreement with the Seminary’s Statement of Faith, Mission, Strategic Vision, and Ethos statement is required.</div><div><br></div><ul><li>Candidate will demonstrate competence in the study and teaching of the Hebrew Bible, including but not limited to hermeneutics, exegesis, and Biblical Hebrew language.</li><li>Teach and advise students in Seminary courses in Biblical Studies, provide academic oversight of students, will pursue scholarly and professional development, serve on departmental and Seminary committees as needed, and work collegially with Seminary faculty and local stakeholders.</li><li>Candidate will demonstrate a commitment to support and respect the Brethren Church heritage, commit to theological education delivered from a Christ-centered worldview, express a strong commitment to a servant-leadership model.</li><li>Deliver courses in multiple formats, whether in-person, hybrid, fully online, or intensive. Courses may be scheduled during the daytime, evenings, and/or weekends.</li><li>Expected to participate in all relevant Seminary student and faculty academic activities.</li><li>Represent the Seminary and engage in community activities that promote theological education and Christian practices.</li></ul> Seminary https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8603 2026-07-13T16:39:28-04:00 2026-07-13T16:39:28-04:00 Part-Time PM Pasta - Student Dining <ul><li>Prepare pasta, sauces, breadsticks, and toppings needed for daily production.</li><li>Complete related paperwork to document accurate product usage and temp logs.</li><li>Maintaining safe food temperatures throughout meal period. Rotation of product, clean up and sanitation of area during and after shift.</li><li>Perform other duties as requested by management.</li></ul> Convocation Center (Student Dining) https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8742 2026-08-21T11:56:20-04:00 2026-08-21T11:56:20-04:00 Full-Time PM Cook - Student Dining <ul><li>Position works 11:00 a.m. - 7:30 p.m. and every other weekend preparing items for the Student Dining hall, Catering, and concession events.</li><li>Works with a team of other members to prepare food that is prepared fresh and to our standards.</li><li>Based on menu mix this position may need to work specific grill positions.</li><li>Benefits available include vacation, sick time, holiday pay, medical and much more.</li></ul> Convocation Center (Student Dining) https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8646 2026-07-28T09:17:23-04:00 2026-07-28T09:17:24-04:00 Assistant Professor of Practical Theology - Ashland Theological Seminary <div><strong>Ethos of Ashland Theological Seminary</strong><br>Ashland Theological Seminary, founded by the Brethren Church, allows its Anabaptist and Pietist heritage to shape the core values of the Seminary. The Seminary is an evangelical and ecumenical institution, as well as a community of faith with an identity shaped by its service to the scholarly community, the church, and the world. We embrace a diversity that finds its unity in Jesus Christ. We practice justice in our engagement with one another and with the world. As partners in ministry and brothers and sisters in Christ, we strive to foster a redemptive community that lives by the values of God's kingdom.<br><br>Ashland Theological Seminary (ATS) is a graduate division of Ashland University, located in Ashland, Ohio. ATS seeks a qualified candidate in Practical Theology. This nine-month, full-time, tenure-track Jack Miller Endowed faculty position in Practical Theology begins on August 1, 2026.<br><br></div><ul><li>Faculty deliver courses in multiple formats, including in-person, hybrid, intensive, and online.</li><li>The person in this role is expected to represent the Seminary and University while engaging in community activities that promote theological education and Christian practices.</li><li>The successful candidate demonstrates a knowledge of and commitment to the Brethren Church heritage and theological education delivered from a Christ-centered worldview, expresses a strong commitment to a servant-leadership model, and a demonstrates the ability to succeed in this role.</li><li>Faculty represent the Seminary and University while they engage in community activities that promote theological education and Christian practices.</li><li>Faculty teach and advise students in graduate and undergraduate core and advanced Practical Theology courses, provide professional guidance to students, participate in scholarly and professional development activities, serve on Seminary departmental and Seminary committees, and work collegially with Seminary and University faculty and administration.</li><li>The successful candidate will have experience/skills in some or all of the following areas: homiletics, worship, spiritual formation, pastoral theology, and church and culture.</li></ul> Seminary"
    },
    "https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/search.atom?utf8=%E2%9C%93&query=&query_v0_posted_at_date=&query_position_type_id%5B%5D=3&435=&query_organizational_tier_3_id%5B%5D=any&1615=&commit=Search": {
      "title": "Ashland University: All Jobs",
      "description": "tag:jobs.ashland.edu,2005:/postings/search Ashland University: All Jobs 2026-08-24T15:40:17-04:00 https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8766 2026-08-24T15:40:16-04:00 2026-08-24T15:40:17-04:00 Principal Faculty for the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies- Part Time - Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences <div>The Part-Time Principal Faculty member for the Master of Science in Physician Assistant Studies Program will work closely with the Program Director and Principal Faculty members to implement and maintain the curriculum in accordance with ARC-PA Standards as a course director on a twelve (12) month, part-time basis. As a Course Director the individual is responsible for development, implementation, delivery, and evaluation of assigned courses. The Principal Faculty works collaboratively with faculty within the Dwight Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences and Ashland University.<br><br>The Part-Time Principal Faculty member is responsible for course development and implementation to ensure the PA students readiness to practice upon graduation.<br><br></div><div><strong>Principal Faculty member responsibilities include:</strong></div><ul><li>Support the mission of Ashland University and Dwight Schar College of Nursing and Health Sciences.</li><li>Support Ashland University’s philosophy of <em>Accent on the Individual.</em></li><li>Development and review of the mission statement of the PA Program.</li><li>Provide academic instruction.</li><li>Participates in review and revision of the program competencies.</li><li>Develops, implements, evaluates and ensures course syllabi maintain compliance with ARC-PA Standards of assigned courses.</li><li>Review and revision, as necessary, of the program goals and competencies.</li><li>Participates in developing, reviewing, and revising as necessary the mission statement for the program.</li><li>Participates in evaluating student performances.</li><li>Participate in the program’s ongoing self-assessment, analysis, and accreditation processes with primary responsibility for didactic education components.</li><li>Is familiar with ARC-PA accreditation standards and assists in providing documented compliance.</li><li>Participate in the development and maintenance of the didactic year sections of the student handbook.</li><li>Participate in the design and implementation of summative examinations.</li><li>Serve as an academic advisor to students.</li><li>Provide remedial instruction of didactic year students.</li><li>Participate in the admissions process including student recruitment and selection.</li><li>Participate as a member of PA program committees as assigned by the PA Program Director.</li><li>Participate in state and national PA organizations as necessary to promote the program and the profession.</li><li>Participates in professional development activities outside of Ashland University’s PA program in areas of clinical practice, scholarly activities or advancement of educational degree as agreed upon by the Program Director.</li><li>Agrees to not participate as a health care provider for students in the program, except in an emergency situation.</li><li>Perform other duties as determined by negotiation at the annual performance review by the Program Director.</li></ul> Medical Sciences https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8735 2026-08-19T12:32:48-04:00 2026-08-19T12:32:49-04:00 Assistant Professor of Biblical Studies - Ashland Theological Seminary <div>Ashland Theological Seminary (ATS) is a graduate division of Ashland University, located in Ashland, Ohio. The position is a full-time, tenure-track faculty position in Biblical Studies. This nine-month position begins on <strong>August 23, 2027</strong>.<br><br></div><div><strong>Ethos of Ashland Theological Seminary</strong></div><div>ATS was founded by the Brethren Church, whose Anabaptist and Pietist heritage shapes the core values of the Seminary. The Seminary is an evangelical and ecumenical institution, as well as a community of faith whose identity is shaped by its service to the scholarly community, the church, and the world. We embrace a diversity that finds its unity in Jesus Christ. We are committed to practicing justice in our engagement with one another and with the world. As partners in ministry and brothers and sisters in Christ, we strive to foster a redemptive community that lives by the values of God's kingdom.<br><br></div><div>Agreement with the Seminary’s Statement of Faith, Mission, Strategic Vision, and Ethos statement is required.</div><div><br></div><ul><li>Candidate will demonstrate competence in the study and teaching of the Hebrew Bible, including but not limited to hermeneutics, exegesis, and Biblical Hebrew language.</li><li>Teach and advise students in Seminary courses in Biblical Studies, provide academic oversight of students, will pursue scholarly and professional development, serve on departmental and Seminary committees as needed, and work collegially with Seminary faculty and local stakeholders.</li><li>Candidate will demonstrate a commitment to support and respect the Brethren Church heritage, commit to theological education delivered from a Christ-centered worldview, express a strong commitment to a servant-leadership model.</li><li>Deliver courses in multiple formats, whether in-person, hybrid, fully online, or intensive. Courses may be scheduled during the daytime, evenings, and/or weekends.</li><li>Expected to participate in all relevant Seminary student and faculty academic activities.</li><li>Represent the Seminary and engage in community activities that promote theological education and Christian practices.</li></ul> Seminary https://jobs.ashland.edu/postings/8646 2026-07-28T09:17:23-04:00 2026-07-28T09:17:24-04:00 Assistant Professor of Practical Theology - Ashland Theological Seminary <div><strong>Ethos of Ashland Theological Seminary</strong><br>Ashland Theological Seminary, founded by the Brethren Church, allows its Anabaptist and Pietist heritage to shape the core values of the Seminary. The Seminary is an evangelical and ecumenical institution, as well as a community of faith with an identity shaped by its service to the scholarly community, the church, and the world. We embrace a diversity that finds its unity in Jesus Christ. We practice justice in our engagement with one another and with the world. As partners in ministry and brothers and sisters in Christ, we strive to foster a redemptive community that lives by the values of God's kingdom.<br><br>Ashland Theological Seminary (ATS) is a graduate division of Ashland University, located in Ashland, Ohio. ATS seeks a qualified candidate in Practical Theology. This nine-month, full-time, tenure-track Jack Miller Endowed faculty position in Practical Theology begins on August 1, 2026.<br><br></div><ul><li>Faculty deliver courses in multiple formats, including in-person, hybrid, intensive, and online.</li><li>The person in this role is expected to represent the Seminary and University while engaging in community activities that promote theological education and Christian practices.</li><li>The successful candidate demonstrates a knowledge of and commitment to the Brethren Church heritage and theological education delivered from a Christ-centered worldview, expresses a strong commitment to a servant-leadership model, and a demonstrates the ability to succeed in this role.</li><li>Faculty represent the Seminary and University while they engage in community activities that promote theological education and Christian practices.</li><li>Faculty teach and advise students in graduate and undergraduate core and advanced Practical Theology courses, provide professional guidance to students, participate in scholarly and professional development activities, serve on Seminary departmental and Seminary committees, and work collegially with Seminary and University faculty and administration.</li><li>The successful candidate will have experience/skills in some or all of the following areas: homiletics, worship, spiritual formation, pastoral theology, and church and culture.</li></ul> Seminary"
